/- Remark 14.26.4: any functor sends a simplicial homotopy `H : Homotopy a b` to the induced
simplicial homotopy between the whiskered morphisms of simplicial objects. Consequently the finite
zigzag relation generated by directed simplicial homotopies is preserved by functors; in the
presence of finite coproducts this also preserves the older coproduct-based notion of homotopy. -/
recall Homotopy.whiskerRight
    (H : Homotopy a b) {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] (F : C ⥤ D) :
  Homotopy (Functor.whiskerRight a F) (Functor.whiskerRight b F)

